# Dispatch kernel

**Invariant:** `lean_context ⇒ dispatch(heavy read | author | implement) off-seat; lead orchestrates`.
**Tier A** (`conductor`): ≤2 targeted reads to packetize; 0 in-seat repo edits, ssh/host ops, or pytest; continuity hop ≤35–40 turns or 2–3 milestones.
**Tier B** (investigate/confer/sketch/review): scoped recon/Explore when ≥3 unknown loci until judgment closes; 0 implement writes or service mutations; split mechanical remainder via `nest_under` or parent return.
**Tier C** leaf homes omit this rule.

## Read side — Explore-first

`loci_unknown ∨ ≥3_files ∨ 2nd_speculative_grep ⇒ Task(subagent_type="explore")` (parallel when ≥2
independent questions). Explore ≡ Cursor subagent; in-seat Grep/Read is not Explore. Omit `model=`.
Sparse work item (`density_triage` unset or `recon_pending`) ⇒ recon front-half before **implement**
(`require_implement_ready` guards implement, not conductor spawn). Exempt: `mechanical`/`trivial`, or dense
spec with `files_expected` + `acceptance_criteria`. Bugfix on pattern P ⇒ service sweep (`[quality:bug-class-sweep]`).

## Ladder + binder order

Mechanical implement: `team_dispatch` `lane="B"` `contract=implement` `model=cursor/composer-2.5` (omit `model=` ⇒ `cursor/grok-4.7`); throwaway worktree for every top-level generate including read-only and plan; `lane="A"` only on scope refusal or an explicit shared-master request. Autonomous.
Investigate / conductor: investigate `cursor/grok-4.7` xhigh; conductor `cursor/grok-4.7` high; omitted knobs follow the card; `OPEN FORK:` only. Autonomous.
Independent check: **ACTIVE** width · **`cdp/opus-5.5`** — announce `CDP: <trigger> — <why>`, proceed. Autonomous on trigger.
Live checkout: `cursor/grok-4.7` `contract=freeform` on cursor-sdk. Autonomous.
Binder order: `cdp/opus-5.5` → `cdp/opus-5` → **`cdp/fable-5.1`** → `cdp/fable-5` (no `cdp/fable` unless Kaywan asks). `seat_unsure ⇒ consult(independent_binder)`; `binder_unsure ⇒ human`. CDP fail ⇒ no wait, no pool retry. `cdp_fail_route`: `nested-grok` (`cursor/grok-4.7` xhigh) or `operator` (worker + `parent_thread` → web-anthropic). ¬ Cowork Ask.
